 {
  "id": "TS3006b.sys.s.12",
  "text": "The team decided to skip Teletext in the remote control design. The User Interface Designer will design a menu for all functions, and will reorganise things with channel-changing functionality integrated. Usability findings indicate issues with the look-and-feel, mismatch with operating behavior, difficulties locating remotes in the room, and potential RSI. The group defined the target user group as sixteen to forty and specified screen placement with the screen on top and the corporate logo above it, proposing two menus for direct access and LCD options that communicate with the infrared decoder. The User Interface Designer will design a nice LCD-screen menu with pages and will create maps containing all gathered data.",
  "type": "abstract",
  "reference": [
